(>> 6.1 Planar Kinematics: Translation, Fixed Rotation, and General Motion) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(A rigid body in planar motion experiences three distinct kinematic modes:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Pure Translation: Every straight line in the body remains strictly parallel to) Tj
T*
(its original direction. All points possess identical velocity and acceleration) Tj
T*
(vectors at any instant: v_A = v_B, and a_A = a_B.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Fixed-Axis Rotation: All particles move in concentric circular paths about a) Tj
T*
(stationary fixed axis perpendicular to the plane of motion. The kinematics are) Tj
T*
(defined by angular displacement theta\(t\), angular velocity omega = dtheta/dt, and) Tj
T*
(angular acceleration alpha = domega/dt.) Tj
T*
(- Linear Velocity: v = r * omega \(directed tangentially\).) Tj
T*
(- Tangential Acceleration: a_t = r * alpha.) Tj
T*
(- Normal \(Centripetal\) Acceleration: a_n = r * omega^2 = v^2 / r.) Tj
T*
(- Total Linear Acceleration: a = sqrt\( a_t^2 + a_n^2 \) = r * sqrt\( alpha^2 + omega^4 \).) Tj
T*
(* 3. General Plane Motion: A simultaneous combination of translation and rotation:) Tj
T*
(v_B = v_A + v_B/A, where v_B/A = omega x r_B/A.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.2 Instantaneous Centre of Zero Velocity \(ICR / ICZ\)) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(At any given instant, the general planar motion of a rigid body can be conceptualized as) Tj
T*
(a pure rotation about a single point in the plane having ZERO linear velocity, termed) Tj
T*
(the Instantaneous Centre of Rotation \(ICR\):) Tj
T*
(* Locating the ICR:) Tj
T*
(- Case 1: If velocities v_A and v_B at two distinct points A and B are known in) Tj
T*
(direction \(non-parallel\), the ICR is the geometric intersection of perpendicular lines) Tj
T*
(drawn to v_A and v_B.) Tj
T*
(- Case 2: For a cylinder or wheel rolling WITHOUT SLIPPING on a stationary surface, the) Tj
T*
(contact point is instantaneously at rest. Hence, the contact point is the ICR.) Tj
T*
(* Velocity Distribution from ICR: Once ICR is found, the velocity of ANY point P on) Tj
T*
(the body is: v_P = omega * r_P/ICR, directed perpendicular to line P-ICR.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.3 Kinetics of Rigid Bodies: Equations of Motion) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(For a rigid body of mass m with centre of mass G subjected to general coplanar force) Tj
T*
(systems:) Tj
T*
(* Translational Equations of Motion: Sigma Fx = m * a_Gx, and Sigma Fy = m * a_Gy.) Tj
T*
(* Rotational Equation of Motion: Sigma M_G = I_G * alpha, where I_G is the mass) Tj
T*
(moment of inertia about the centroidal z-axis.) Tj
T*
(* Alternative Moment Equation about arbitrary point P: Sigma M_P = I_G * alpha + \(m *) Tj
T*
(a_G\) * d.) Tj
T*
ET

