T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A reciprocating slider-crank mechanism has a crank OA of length r = 150) Tj
T*
(mm rotating counterclockwise at constant speed N = 300 RPM \(omega = 31.42 rad/s\).) Tj
T*
(Connecting rod AB has length L = 500 mm. At the instant when crank OA makes theta = 60) Tj
T*
(deg with the horizontal line of slider stroke, calculate: \(1\) Linear velocity of crank) Tj
T*
(pin A, \(2\) Angular velocity omega_AB of the connecting rod, \(3\) Linear velocity of) Tj
T*
(slider B.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Linear Velocity of Crank Pin A:) Tj
T*
(v_A = r * omega = 0.150 m * 31.42 rad/s = 4.71 m/s.) Tj
T*
(Direction of v_A: Perpendicular to crank OA \(at angle 60 + 90 = 150 deg\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Establish Geometry and Locate ICR of Rod AB:) Tj
T*
(Slider B is constrained to move horizontally along the stroke axis => velocity v_B is) Tj
T*
(strictly horizontal.) Tj
T*
(- Draw perpendicular to v_A at A \(which is line OA extended\).) Tj
T*
(- Draw perpendicular to v_B at B \(which is a vertical line through B\).) Tj
T*
(- Intersection of line OA extended and vertical line through B defines the ICR.) Tj
T*
