(In triangle O-B-ICR:) Tj
T*
(Angle of rod AB with horizontal: In triangle OAB, by sine rule: 0.150 / sin\(beta\) =) Tj
T*
(0.500 / sin\(60\) => sin\(beta\) = 0.150 * 0.8660 / 0.500 = 0.2598 => beta = 15.06 deg.) Tj
T*
(Distance from ICR to A: r_A/ICR = 0.500 * [ cos\(15.06\) / sin\(60\) ] = 0.500 * \(0.9657 /) Tj
T*
(0.8660\) = 0.5576 m.) Tj
T*
(Distance from ICR to B: r_B/ICR = 0.150 * [ sin\(60 + 15.06\) / sin\(60\) ] + ... = 0.4430) Tj
T*
(m.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute Angular Velocity omega_AB and Slider Velocity v_B:) Tj
T*
(omega_AB = v_A / r_A/ICR = 4.71 m/s / 0.5576 m = 8.45 rad/s \(clockwise\).) Tj
T*
(v_B = omega_AB * r_B/ICR = 8.45 rad/s * 0.4430 m = 3.74 m/s.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Crank pin velocity v_A = 4.71 m/s; connecting rod omega_AB = 8.45 rad/s;) Tj
T*
(slider velocity v_B = 3.74 m/s.) Tj
