T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A solid uniform civil drainage concrete pipe section of mass m = 200 kg) Tj
T*
(and outer radius R = 0.40 m \(centroidal MOI I_G = 0.5 * m * R^2\) is released from rest) Tj
T*
(on an incline of theta = 30 deg. Assuming it rolls without slipping, calculate: \(1\)) Tj
T*
(Linear acceleration a_G of its center of mass, \(2\) Minimum coefficient of static) Tj
T*
(friction mu_s required to prevent slipping.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Establish Equations of Motion for Rolling Body:) Tj
T*
(Forces acting: Gravity component down incline m*g*sin\(30\); Normal reaction N =) Tj
T*
(m*g*cos\(30\); Friction force F_s acting up the incline at contact point.) Tj
T*
(Translational equilibrium down incline: m * g * sin\(30\) - F_s = m * a_G. \(Equation 1\)) Tj
T*
(Rotational equilibrium about center G: F_s * R = I_G * alpha. \(Equation 2\)) Tj
T*
(Kinematic rolling condition \(no slip\): a_G = R * alpha => alpha = a_G / R.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Substitute rolling condition into rotational equation:) Tj
T*
(F_s * R = \(0.5 * m * R^2\) * \(a_G / R\) = 0.5 * m * R * a_G => F_s = 0.5 * m * a_G.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Solve for Linear Acceleration a_G:) Tj
T*
(Substitute F_s into Equation 1: m * g * sin\(30\) - 0.5 * m * a_G = m * a_G.) Tj
T*
(1.5 * m * a_G = m * g * sin\(30\) => a_G = \(2/3\) * g * sin\(30\).) Tj
T*
(a_G = \(2/3\) * 9.81 * 0.50 = 3.27 m/s^2.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Calculate Friction Force and Minimum Friction Coefficient:) Tj
T*
(F_s = 0.5 * 200 * 3.27 = 327.0 N.) Tj
T*
(Normal Reaction: N = m * g * cos\(30\) = 200 * 9.81 * 0.8660 = 1699.1 N.) Tj
T*
(Condition for no slip: F_s <= mu_s * N => mu_s >= F_s / N.) Tj
T*
(mu_s >= 327.0 / 1699.1 = 0.1925 \(or mu_s >= tan\(30\) / 3 = 0.5774 / 3 = 0.1925\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Acceleration a_G = 3.27 m/s^2; Minimum coefficient of static friction mu_s =) Tj
T*
(0.193.) Tj
T*
() Tj
