(Problem Context: A heavy cast-iron flywheel of mass m = 500 kg and radius of gyration k) Tj
T*
(= 0.60 m rotates at N1 = 600 RPM. A mechanical friction brake is applied, exerting a) Tj
T*
(constant retarding braking torque of T_brake = 180 N-m. Determine: \(1\) Initial kinetic) Tj
T*
(energy of the flywheel, \(2\) Angular deceleration alpha, \(3\) Time t required to bring the) Tj
T*
(flywheel to rest, \(4\) Total revolutions N_rev turned during braking.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Mass Moment of Inertia I_G and Initial Angular Velocity omega_1:) Tj
T*
(I_G = m * k^2 = 500 * \(0.60\)^2 = 500 * 0.36 = 180.0 kg-m^2.) Tj
T*
(omega_1 = \(2 * pi * N1\) / 60 = \(2 * pi * 600\) / 60 = 20 * pi = 62.83 rad/s.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Initial Kinetic Energy KE_1:) Tj
T*
(KE_1 = 0.5 * I_G * \(omega_1\)^2 = 0.5 * 180.0 * \(62.83\)^2 = 90.0 * 3947.84 = 355,305.6 J) Tj
T*
(= 355.31 kJ.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Angular Deceleration alpha:) Tj
T*
(T_brake = I_G * alpha => alpha = T_brake / I_G = 180 N-m / 180 kg-m^2 = 1.0 rad/s^2) Tj
T*
(\(retarding\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Stopping Time t and Revolutions N_rev:) Tj
T*
(omega_2 = omega_1 - alpha * t => 0 = 62.83 - 1.0 * t => t = 62.83 s \(approx 1 minute 3) Tj
T*
(seconds\).) Tj
T*
(Total angular displacement: Delta theta = \(omega_1\)^2 / \(2 * alpha\) = \(62.83\)^2 / \(2 *) Tj
T*
(1.0\) = 1973.92 radians.) Tj
T*
(Number of revolutions: N_rev = Delta theta / \(2 * pi\) = 1973.92 / 6.2832 = 314.16) Tj
T*
(revolutions.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: KE_initial = 355.31 kJ; stopping time t = 62.83 s; revolutions turned =) Tj
T*
(314.16 rev.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
