([EXAMPLE 4: Swinging Slender Structural Rod Released from Rest]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A uniform slender steel member AB of mass m = 24 kg and length L = 2.0) Tj
T*
(m is hinged at end A and held horizontally. It is released from rest. At the instant it) Tj
T*
(swings through the vertical position, calculate: \(1\) Angular velocity omega, \(2\) Angular) Tj
T*
(acceleration alpha, \(3\) Total hinge reaction force at A.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Conservation of Energy between horizontal \(1\) and vertical \(2\):) Tj
T*
(Hinge MOI for slender rod: I_A = \(1/3\) * m * L^2 = \(1/3\) * 24 * \(2.0\)^2 = 32.0 kg-m^2.) Tj
T*
(Vertical drop of center of mass G: Delta h = L / 2 = 2.0 / 2 = 1.0 m.) Tj
T*
(Potential energy loss = m * g * Delta h = 24 * 9.81 * 1.0 = 235.44 J.) Tj
T*
(Kinetic energy in vertical position = 0.5 * I_A * omega^2 = 0.5 * 32.0 * omega^2 = 16.0) Tj
T*
(* omega^2.) Tj
T*
(Equating: 16.0 * omega^2 = 235.44 => omega^2 = 14.715 => omega = sqrt\(14.715\) = 3.84) Tj
T*
(rad/s.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Angular Acceleration alpha in vertical position:) Tj
T*
(In vertical position, line of gravity force passes directly through hinge pin A =>) Tj
T*
(Moment arm d = 0.) Tj
T*
(Sigma M_A = m * g * 0 = 0 => alpha = 0 rad/s^2.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Reaction Force at Hinge A in vertical position:) Tj
T*
(Center of mass G experiences centripetal acceleration upward toward hinge A:) Tj
T*
