(>> 6.6 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Define the Instantaneous Centre of Rotation \(ICR\) and explain how it is used to) Tj
T*
(determine velocity distribution in a planar mechanism.) Tj
T*
(Answer: The Instantaneous Centre of Rotation is a unique point in the plane of a rigid) Tj
T*
(body experiencing general planar motion that instantaneously possesses zero linear) Tj
T*
(velocity. Since its velocity is zero at that particular instant, the complex plane) Tj
T*
(motion \(translation + rotation\) of the body reduces to pure rotation about this ICR. To) Tj
T*
(locate the ICR: if the direction of velocity vectors at two distinct points A and B are) Tj
T*
(known, perpendicular lines drawn to these velocity vectors intersect at the ICR. The) Tj
T*
(magnitude of velocity of any arbitrary point P on the body is then simply v_P = omega *) Tj
T*
(r_P/ICR, and its direction is perpendicular to the radial vector connecting ICR to P.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Derive the general kinetic energy expression for a rigid body undergoing) Tj
T*
(general planar motion.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Consider a rigid body composed of particles of mass m_i with position vector r_i) Tj
T*
(relative to center of mass G. Let G have translational velocity v_G and the body rotate) Tj
T*
(with angular velocity omega. The velocity of particle i is v_i = v_G + \(omega x r_i\).) Tj
T*
(Kinetic energy is: KE = 0.5 * Sigma\(m_i * |v_i|^2\) = 0.5 * Sigma\( m_i * [ v_G^2 +) Tj
T*
(2*v_G*\(omega x r_i\) + |omega x r_i|^2 ] \). Since Integral r_i dm = 0 \(by definition of) Tj
T*
(center of mass\), the cross term vanishes identically. The term Sigma\(m_i * |omega x) Tj
T*
(r_i|^2\) equals I_G * omega^2. Therefore: KE = 0.5 * m * v_G^2 + 0.5 * I_G * omega^2. The) Tj
T*
(total kinetic energy separates neatly into translational energy of the center of mass) Tj
T*
(and rotational energy about the center of mass.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.7 Key Takeaways and Revision Points) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* General planar motion decomposes into translation of center of mass G plus rotation) Tj
T*
(about G.) Tj
T*
(* At the ICR, velocity is zero; v_P = omega * r_P/ICR for every point on the body.) Tj
T*
(* Rolling without slipping has ICR at the instantaneous point of ground contact.) Tj
T*
(* Kinetic energy of rolling body combines translation and rotation: KE = 0.5*m*v_G^2) Tj
T*
(+ 0.5*I_G*omega^2.) Tj
